       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the maximum labeled metformin dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also above the usual maximum for one administration, which is about 850 mg of immediate-release metformin. At this dose the risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThe intended dose may have been one of these:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release metformin.\n- **1,700 mg per day, divided.** For example, 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** at some other frequency.\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
